cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spectral-trust in your work, please cite the software as below."
type: software
title: "spectral-trust: graph-spectral diagnostics for transformer attention"
version: 0.4.1
authors:
  - family-names: "Noël"
    given-names: "Valentin"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/vcnoel/spectral-trust"
url: "https://github.com/vcnoel/spectral-trust"
abstract: >-
  A Python library that builds graphs from a transformer's attention weights
  and computes spectral diagnostics on them: Laplacian eigenvalues, algebraic
  connectivity (the Fiedler value), Dirichlet energy and the high-frequency
  energy ratio of the residual stream, per layer or per head.
keywords:
  - graph signal processing
  - spectral graph theory
  - attention
  - transformers
  - interpretability
